---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import BrandLogo from '../components/BrandLogo.astro';
import ModelDiagram from '../components/ModelDiagram.astro';
import { codeToHtml } from 'shiki';
import article from '../../examples/customer-story/models/customer-story.yaml?raw';
const snippet = article.slice(article.indexOf('  - id: customer'), article.indexOf('\neditorial:')).trimEnd();
const code = await codeToHtml(snippet, { lang: 'yaml', themes: { light: 'github-light', dark: 'github-dark' } });
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'A shared language for content models', description: 'A portable format for content models and the intent behind them. Learn CMMF, explore the specification, and work visually in Studio.', template: 'splash', editUrl: false }}>
  <div class="homepage">
    <section class="home-intro" aria-labelledby="_top">
      <div class="home-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Content modelling / a shared foundation</p>
        <h1 id="_top">Keep the intent.<br />Carry the model.</h1>
        <p class="home-lead">A portable format for content models<br class="wide-break" /> and the intent behind them.</p>
        <p class="home-description">Agree what your content needs to do. Describe its structure and relationships in CMMF. Carry those decisions into your CMS implementation.</p>
        <div class="home-actions"><a class="primary-action" href="/learn/why-cmmf/">Start with the idea <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-action" href="/spec/1.2.0/">Read the specification <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="home-identity"><BrandLogo expanded /><div class="mobile-identity"><BrandLogo /><p>Content Model Master Format</p></div><p class="identity-note">Structure. Relationships. Editorial intent.</p></div>
    </section>
    <div class="workflow" aria-label="From modelling intent to implementation">
      <div><span class="step-number">01</span><div><strong>Agree the intent</strong><p>Start with the people and the content.</p></div></div>
      <div><span class="step-number">02</span><div><strong>Describe the model</strong><p>Make structure and relationships explicit.</p></div></div>
      <div><span class="step-number">03</span><div><strong>Translate deliberately</strong><p>Record decisions for your chosen CMS.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <section class="home-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A model you can reason about</p><h2 id="example-title">One story. Two different relationships.</h2><p class="reading">A customer can appear in many stories. A quotation belongs in the context of one story. A useful model makes that distinction visible before a CMS makes it for you.</p></div>
      <div class="example-grid"><ModelDiagram /><div class="example-code"><div class="code-label"><span>customer-story.yaml · relationship excerpt</span><span>CMMF 1.2.0</span></div><Fragment set:html={code} /><p>This excerpt comes from the complete Customer Story tutorial model.</p><a href="/examples/customer-story/">Explore the files and decisions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="home-translation" aria-labelledby="translation-title"><p class="eyebrow">From shared intent to a working system</p><h2 id="translation-title">The model carries the meaning.<br />Translation records the choices.</h2><p class="reading">A reference may become a CMS relationship field. An embedded object may become a nested group. CMMF describes the intended structure; your implementation records what the platform can represent and where compromises enter.</p><a class="text-action" href="/docs/concepts/translation/">Understand translation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
    <section class="home-paths" aria-labelledby="paths-title"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Choose your next step</p><h2 id="paths-title">A format, with tools around it.</h2></div><div class="path-grid">
      <a class="path-card" href="/docs/get-started/first-model/"><span class="path-index">Learn</span><h3>Start with the content</h3><p>Understand the problem, the vocabulary and the modelling decisions.</p><span>Create your first model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>
      <a class="path-card" href="/docs/reference/canonical-types/"><span class="path-index">Reference</span><h3>Find the precise detail</h3><p>Look up field types, read the specification and download the schema.</p><span>Explore the reference <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>
      <a class="path-card studio-card" href="/tools/"><span class="path-index">Tools</span><h3>Work visually or with an agent</h3><p>Explore Studio’s visual editor and the CMMF Skills development release.</p><span>Meet the tools <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>
    </div></section>
    <div class="home-version"><span>Current format <strong>1.2.0</strong></span><a href="/changelog/">What changed <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="https://github.com/headless-company/content-model-master-format">Open format · Apache 2.0 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>
